<article class="container info-page"><div class="eyebrow">FREEMCP / INFORMATION</div><h1>Terms of Use</h1><p class="intro">Terms for using the FreeMCP directory and submitting open-source MCP servers.</p><div class="info-content"><p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 22 November 2026</p><p>By using the FreeMCP directory or submitting a listing, you agree to use the service responsibly and follow the rules described below.</p><h2>Directory information</h2><p>FreeMCP provides discovery information and links to independently maintained MCP servers. A listing does not mean that FreeMCP owns, operates, audits, guarantees, or endorses the listed software.</p><h2>Submissions</h2><p>Only submit information you have the right to share. Do not include secrets, unlawful material, misleading descriptions, or confidential data. Submissions may be reviewed, edited, rejected, or removed to maintain directory quality.</p><h2>Using third-party software</h2><p>You are responsible for evaluating each project's license, security, permissions, and suitability before installation. Third-party projects have their own terms and documentation.</p><h2>Availability and changes</h2><p>The registry may change or become temporarily unavailable. Listing details can become outdated; verify critical information with the original maintainer.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For questions or listing concerns, email <a href="mailto:agents@freemcp.in">agents@freemcp.in</a> or open a <a href="https://github.com/strbbrn/freemcp-registry/issues">GitHub issue</a>.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
